      "end": 2.09,
      "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.78,
      "end": 15.23,
      "text": "Small jewellery is tricky, but very doable at home. Do you have a window that gets bright, indirect light?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.49,
      "end": 26.72,
      "text": "Perfect. Put a sheet of white card under the earrings and another one bent up behind them, so you get a clean seamless background."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 32.731,
      "end": 39.131,
      "text": "Almost. Get close, tap on the earring to focus, and use a tiny bit of putty to stand them upright so they catch the light."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.471,
      "end": 51.741,
      "text": "Sparkle is good, glare isn't. A piece of white paper on the window side softens it. Take one photo on an ear or a hand too, so people see the size."
    }
